# The shape of a `zone.tree` and a `zone.code.tree`.
#
# `zone.tree` is committed and names what a project needs, never what those things are. `zone.code.tree` is
# gitignored, mirrors the same nesting, and holds the sealed values. One shape covers both, because a declaration and
# its cache reading the same way is what stops the two drifting.
#
# The grammar that produces these is the `zone` role at `@term/mill/code/zone`. The tool that consumes them is
# `@term/zone`. Named `zone-file` rather than `zone` because `./zone` is the view component AST and Term form names
# are package-global.
#
#   base bitwarden
#   need database-url
#   want sentry-dsn
#
#   zone word.surf
#     zone star
#       load star
#       need sentry-dsn

load ./text
  find text

load ./list
  find list

load ./boolean
  find boolean

# One declared requirement. Carries a name and never a value.
#
# `must` is the difference between `need` and `want`: a missing `need` refuses to start the command, a missing `want`
# is fine. `from` is the name this value has at the provider when it differs from the local one. `also` is the extra
# spellings the same value is published under, which is how six names for one secret collapse to one stored value
# without every reader being renamed at once.
form zone-need
  link name, like text
  link must, like boolean
  link from, like text
  link also, like list

# One sealed value, in a `zone.code.tree` only. `code` is the nonce, ciphertext and tag, tone-packed at 32 symbols.
form zone-code
  link name, like text
  link code, like text

# One zone, at any depth. The root is a `zone-hold` with an empty name.
#
# `base` and `bind` are inherited by every zone below. `cast` is a list because a zone may publish the same value
# under more than one spelling, which is how `land` gets both the plain name and the `TF_VAR_` name from one fetch.
form zone-hold
  link name, like text
  link base, like text
  link bind, like text
  link root, like boolean
  link need, like list
  link cast, like list
  link load, like list
  link code, like list
  link zone, like list

# A whole file. The four cache fields are empty in a `zone.tree` and filled in a `zone.code.tree`.
#
# `deck` is the tone code of the sha256 of the `zone.tree` this cache was built from, so a cache built against an
# older declaration is detectable with no key at all.
form zone-file
  link mark, like text
  link made, like text
  link good, like text
  link seal, like text
  link deck, like text
  link hold, like zone-hold
